 The congruence equation is \(x + 4609 \equiv 2104 \pmod{12}\). To solve for \(x\), we can simplify the equation by reducing 4609 and 2104 modulo 12 first. Then we solve for \(x\). Let's do this step by step. First, find \(4609 \mod 12\): \[
4609 \div 12 = 384 \text{ remainder } 1 \implies 4609 \equiv 1 \pmod{12}
\] Next, find \(2104 \mod 12\): \[
2104 \div 12 = 175 \text{ remainder } 4 \implies 2104 \equiv 4 \pmod{12}
\] So the equation simplifies to \[
x + 1 \equiv 4 \pmod{12}
\] By subtracting 1 from both sides, we get \[
x \equiv 3 \pmod{12}
\] The smallest positive integer \(x\) that satisfies this congruence is \(3\). <think> \(3\) </think> <answer> 3 </answer>

